# Ours. 6.1's parenthesis asks this whether a number in brackets begins a
# North American telephone number, which 6.1's Canadian French then reads a
# digit at a time through three rules of its own. Those are not taken: the
# answer here is always no, which is what 6.1's France French answers, and a
# telephone number is read in both Frenches as 4.3 reads it, which in
# Canadian French is a digit at a time already.

rule convert_phone_number takes 3
  bare
  afresh
  answer 1
end

